    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">3.3 Electrical connection</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">A 2-pole screw terminal is provided in the housing for connecting the electrical line. A M16 x 1.5 cable gland serves for entering the cable.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">Observe the applicable reg regulations and safety standards pertaining to the installation and operation of electrical systems as well as the directives and guidelines on explosion protection.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">Do not lay the signal line for measured value transmission close to power lines. Power lines produce interference in their near vicinity which impairs the measured values on the signal line.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">3.4 Temperature sensor without built-in transmitter</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">The Pt 100 measuring element is connected with the screw terminal through 2 wires (see connection diagram Fig. 3-2). The measured value can be transmitted via a 2-wire, a 3-wire or a 4-wire cable. Depending on the number of wires used for this purpose, the wires have to be combined accordingly when they are connected to the screw terminal.</p>
